Currently, it is not possible to set the Selection Tags input element to only accept one selection from the list of choices. Using Velo, you can limit the Selection Tags input element to only allow visitors to choose one selection at a time.

Workaround:
- Go to your Editor.
- Go to the page with the connected Selection Tags element.
- Enable Velo Dev Mode: click Dev Mode at the top of the Editor; click Turn on Dev Mode.
- Replace the gray text with the code below, after the first line: $w.onReady(function () {
$w('#selectionTags1').onChange((event) => {
 const indeces = $w('#selectionTags1').selectedIndices;
 const singleIndex = indeces.slice(-1);
 $w('#selectionTags1').selectedIndices = singleIndex
 })
- If needed, replace selectionTags1 with the ID of your Selection Tags element. Click the relevant Selection Tags element to find its ID in the Properties and Events panel.

Note: Do not remove the hashtag (#) or apostrophes (') in the code.

Currently, Previous/Next navigational buttons on dynamic item pages do not loop. When a visitor reaches the last item page returned by the dataset, the Next button is inactive. When a visitor is on the first item page, the Previous button is inactive. It is not possible, without using Velo code, to have these buttons continue to navigate visitors through all the items.

Workaround: Using Velo, you can create Previous/Next buttons that loop continuously through your dynamic pages. Go to the dynamic item page that has Previous/Next buttons. Make sure the buttons' click actions are not connected to the dataset: select the Previous button, click the Connect to CMS icon, set Click action connects to to Not connected, and repeat for the Next button. Enable Velo Dev Mode. Paste the import statement at the top of your page code and paste the click-handler snippet after $w.onReady(function () {. Replace the button IDs, dataset ID, and first/last page slug placeholders with those used by your site. In the code, do not remove the hashtags (#) or apostrophes ('). To get the correct first and last dynamic item page addresses, create a custom collection view with the same sorting and filtering as in the dataset settings, then copy the URL slug from the [Collection] (Item) page link field in your collection.

Code:
import wixLocationFrontend from 'wix-location-frontend';

$w('#prevBtn').onClick(async () => {
 const previousPage = await $w('#dynamicDataset').getPreviousDynamicPage();
 if (previousPage) { wixLocationFrontend.to(previousPage) }
 else { wixLocationFrontend.to('/last-page-url') }
 })
 $w('#nextBtn').onClick(async () => {
 const nextPage = await $w('#dynamicDataset').getNextDynamicPage();
 if (nextPage) { wixLocationFrontend.to(nextPage) }
 else { wixLocationFrontend.to('/first-page-url') }
 })
